# Gateway trust-store and ACME inventory reads

These are read-only inventory summaries. They do not issue, renew, revoke,
install or validate certificates, change ACME accounts, install plugins, run
automation actions, or prove that a certificate is trusted by a client.

The following routes require firewall.view and retain organization, active
parent and site-access admission before connecting to the gateway:

- GET /firewall/gateways/{id}/certificates
- GET /firewall/gateways/{id}/certificates/cas
- GET /firewall/gateways/{id}/acme
- GET /firewall/gateways/{id}/acme/certificates

Unsupported operations return 501. Unavailable connections, failed component
reads, incomplete pages and malformed responses return a generic 502. An
overview requires every component. A failed component cannot silently become
an empty array in a successful overview. The admitted gateway identity is not
replaced by adapter-supplied metadata. Cancellation remains cancellation, even
when another component has failed. Raw device errors and private key material
must not appear in responses or diagnostic stack traces from these reads.

The OPNsense adapter uses the documented Trust CA search and ACME search actions
for certificates, accounts, validations and actions. It requests all rows where
the search API supports it and requires matching total and returned counts,
page one and unique identities. The documented CRL GET uses the server's default
recordset limit; a truncated answer is refused. CRL search includes CA records,
so only rows indicating a configured CRL are counted as revocation lists. This
is not verification of CRL content, validity, distribution or revocation status.

ACME settings are read from acmeclient.settings, including the selected values
of the environment and log-level options. Normalized public fields exclude
account credentials, private keys and plugin-specific secret configuration.
The certificate search does not establish private-key presence; an absent key
field must not be interpreted as confirmation that no private key exists.

The dashboard validates gateway identity, inventory shapes and counts. It shows
loading while refreshing, hides stale counts after a failure, and offers an
explicit retry. An empty state requires a complete successful inventory. ACME
row badges describe whether configuration is enabled; they do not assert that
issuance, validation or renewal succeeded. All four ACME lists must be empty
before the overview is described as empty.

Compatibility is version-specific. These contracts follow the OPNsense API
documentation and reviewed upstream controller/model source. A response from a
different firmware or plugin version may be refused rather than guessed.
Validate the release image against the exact firmware, os-acme-client version
and read privileges you intend to support before claiming hardware acceptance.

Regression checks use real PostgreSQL/ASGI and the actual HTTP client/parser
with synthetic device transport and identity fixtures. Separate frontend tests
exercise the real page/query components. These are not live device acceptance,
normal-login hardware tests, continuous monitoring, CA-chain verification,
renewal automation, a recovery guarantee or enterprise certification.

The independent expiry inventory is described in CERTIFICATE-INVENTORY-READS.
Gateway backup restore remains a separate capability and acceptance gate.

